[1.080308, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.670544, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n"]
[1.670669, "o", "  identity: mnid:092fdaa10942529e480d04b761b273d0b6e285619686fc54c33b4913b80a8f84\r\n"]
[1.670716, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled — private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/3bb88e636d2c12351f583bd14c4aba36dd5a457d50edd3b821073499cdb1154a.key\r\n  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n\r\n"]
[1.670762, "o", "  mnema writes no file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n  project in a file of its own — the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names — and\r\n"]
[1.670775, "o", "  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n"]
[1.670835, "o", "  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n    @MNEMA.md\r\n"]
[1.670913, "o", "\r\n"]
[1.670929, "o", "  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.285806, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
